WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:02.290
October was a beautiful month at Green Gables.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.130
Oh, Marilla, I'm so glad I live in a world
where there are Octobers.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.800
It would be terrible if we just skipped from
September to November, wouldn't it?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.420
Look at these maple branches.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.240
Don't they give you a thrill?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.550
I'm going to decorate my room with them.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:42.950
Messy things.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.600
You clutter up your room entirely too much
with out-of-doors stuff, Anne.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.660
Bedrooms were made to sleep in.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.940
Oh, and dream in too, Marilla.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.570
And one can dream so much better in
a room where there are pretty things.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:03.270
I'm going to put these boughs in the old
blue jug and set them on my table.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.340
Mind you don't drop leaves
all over the stairs then.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:08.350
All right!

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.220
Anne! Anne!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.340
I'm coming!

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.110
What's the matter?

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.520
This afternoon, I'm...

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:40.690
going on a meeting of the Aid Society at
Carmody and I won't be home before dark.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.830
You'll have to get Matthew
and Jerry their supper.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.870
You just have to warm this up
before they come.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.550
So mind you don't forget to put the
tea to draw as you did last time.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:57.630
I won't forget this time.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.810
And Matthew was so good.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.820
He never scolded a bit. I...

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.600
Matthew would think it all right if
you took a notion to get up and

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.440
have dinner in the middle of the night.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:15.240
And... I don't really know if I'm doing right...

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.910
It may make you more addlepated than ever

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.520
but you can ask Diana to come over

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.810
and spend the afternoon with
you and have tea here.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.720
Oh, Marilla!

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:27.810
How perfectly lovely!

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.690
You are able to imagine things after all

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:35.140
or else you'd never have understood how
I've longed for that very thing.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.910
It will seem so nice and grown-uppish.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.160
No fear of my forgetting to put the tea
to draw when I have company.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:54.350
Oh, Marilla, can I use the
rosebud spray tea set?

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.330
No, indeed! The rosebud tea set!

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.160
Well, what next?

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.810
You know I never use that except
for the minister or the Aids.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.820
But you can open the little yellow
crock of cherry preserves.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.980
It's time it was being used anyhow.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.520
And you can have fruit cake and cookies.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:20.590
I can just imagine myself sitting down at the
head of the table and pouring out the tea.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:24.130
And asking Diana if she takes sugar!

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:29.830
I know she doesn't but of course I'll
ask her just as if I didn't know.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:56.180
Oh, Marilla, can I take her into the spare
room to lay off her hat when she comes?

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.870
And then into the parlor to sit?

00:05:58.870 --> 00:05:59.970
No.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.990
The sitting room will do for
you and your company.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.000
But there's a bottle of raspberry
cordial that was left over

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.120
from the church social the other night.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.650
You can have it.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.970
It's on the second shelf of
the sitting-room closet.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.500
Raspberry cordial? Can I really have it?

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.120
Good morning, Anne!

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.010
Good morning, Mrs. Barry!

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.830
Is Diana back already?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:38.040
Yes. she's cleaning
her shoes in the house.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.190
Thank you!

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:58.380
If you don't take off your hands, I'll clean
the shoe in your face, Minnie May.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.200
It's Anne!

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.140
That's right!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:02.780
Anne!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.100
Then do you know why I'm here?

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.060
Of course, to play.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:09.500
Wrong!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.320
I came to ask you for tea.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.470
Really? For tea?

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:23.290
I cordially invite you to Green Gables this
afternoon, Miss Diana Barry.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.330
Then, just after
Marilla had driven off,

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:42.300
Diana came over to Green Gables,
dressed in her second-best dress.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.440
Oh, welcome to my humble abode,
Miss Diana Barry.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:04.270
Thank you for your invitation,
Miss Anne Shirley.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:05.930
You are too kind.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.020
Please come in.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:15.640
Please.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.230
I'm sorry for intruding.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.660
Pretend this is the sitting room.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:25.580
How is your mother?

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.120
She is very well, thank you.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.190
And how is Mr. Cuthbert?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.840
He is hauling potatoes
to the Lily Sands.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.520
Our potato crop is very good this year.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:37.730
How is your father's crop?

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.780
It is fairly good.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:43.030
Have you picked many of your apples yet?

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:44.980
Yes, ever so many.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.660
Let's go get some of the
Red Sweetings, Diana.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.060
Marilla says we can have
all that are left on the tree.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.530
How wonderful!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.380
Be careful.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.080
Yes.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.170
Are you thirsty, Diana?

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.180
Would you like a bright red
drink before the tea?

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.910
What is it?
I can drink something before.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.730
I'm going to get it now, wait for me.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:06.050
It's not here.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:14.820
It must be that one!

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.570
I'm sorry, please wait a moment.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:33.280
My, it looks delicious!
It's raspberry cordial, isn't it?

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:34.430
You're right!

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:38.030
Now, please help yourself.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.560
What about you?

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:43.890
I don't feel as if I wanted any
after all those apples.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.890
I'll have some then.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.780
That's awfully nice raspberry cordial.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:13.140
I didn't know raspberry cordial was so nice.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:18.740
It's ever so much nicer than Mrs. Lynde's,
although she brags of hers so much.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.520
It doesn't taste a bit like hers.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:24.810
Marilla's raspberry cordial is
probably much nicer than Mrs. Lynde's.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:27.310
Marilla is a famous cook.

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.870
Right, I have to prepare the tea.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.810
Drink as much as you like.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:46.990
Marilla is trying to teach me to cook
but I assure you, it is uphill work.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.470
There's so little scope for
imagination in cookery.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.120
You just have to go
by rules, right?

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.720
The last time I forgot to put the flour in.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:12:00.180
I was thinking the loveliest
sad story about you and me.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.270
A lovely sad story?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.870
What story is that?
Tell me!

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.900
I imagined...

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.800
Oh, no.
I forgot about the water.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.800
You were desperately ill with smallpox.

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.110
And everybody deserted you,

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:24.530
but I went boldly to your bedside
and nursed you back to life.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.080
And then I took the smallpox and died.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:35.530
And I was buried under those
poplar trees in the graveyard.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.200
It's a very sad story.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:48.410
You planted a rosebush by my grave
and watered it with your tears.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:55.860
And you never forgot the friend of your
youth who sacrificed her life for you.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:00.030
Oh, it was such a pathetic tale.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:03.020
The tears just rained down over my cheeks.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:05.770
But I forgot to put the flour

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:10.040
and the cake was a dismal failure.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.830
Diana, what is the matter?

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:23.890
I'm... I'm awful sick.
I must go right home.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.260
Oh, you mustn't dream of going
home without your tea!

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.050
I'll get it right off!

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:31.420
I must go home.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:36.020
Let me give you a bit of fruit cake and
some of the cherry preserves.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.290
Lie down on the sofa for
a little while and you'll be better.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.970
Where do you feel bad?

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:43.620
I must go home.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:49.530
I never heard of company
going home without tea.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:53.420
Diana, do you suppose that you're
really taking the smallpox?

00:13:55.780 --> 00:14:00.120
If you are, I'll go and nurse you,
you can depend on that.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.180
I'll never forsake you.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:07.060
But, Diana, I do wish you'd stay till after tea.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.360
Where do you feel bad?

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.130
I'm awful dizzy.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:16.370
Hat!

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.080
I'll get it for you!

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.390
I must go home.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.060
My hat.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:56.360
I like you!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:02.860
That's enough!

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:44.690
The next day was Sunday and it rained all day.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:49.260
Anne's heart was as the weather.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.320
Diana...

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.770
And on the next afternoon...

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:11.310
I sent Anne down to Rachel's on an errand.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.570
I wanted her to relax a little.
She seemed worried.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:21.450
She didn't tell me anything but she and
Diana must have argued with each other.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:31.890
Whatever has gone wrong now?

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:38.110
I do hope you haven't gone and
been saucy to Mrs. Lynde again.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.430
Anne Shirley,

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.030
when I ask you a question
I want to be answered.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.660
Sit right up and tell me
what you are crying about.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:03.600
Mrs. Lynde was up to see Mrs. Barry today

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.950
and Mrs. Barry was in an awful
state because of me.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.810
What did you do to Diana?

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:20.270
She says that I set Diana drunk Saturday and
sent her home in a disgraceful condition.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.470
And that I must be a bad, wicked girl

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:26.070
and she's never going to let
Diana play with me again.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:30.770
Oh, Marilla, I'm just overcome with woe.

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:32.740
Set Diana drunk!

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:33.740
You...

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.130
What on earth did you give her?

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:39.770
Raspberry cordial.

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:44.160
I never thought raspberry cordial
would set people drunk.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.280
Not even if they drank three tumblerfuls.

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:48.670
Three tumblerfuls?

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:52.480
But I didn't mean to set her drunk.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.800
Drunk fiddlesticks!

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.460
Mrs. Barry must be crazy.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:14.210
Anne, you certainly have a
genius for getting into trouble.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:20.490
You went and gave Diana currant wine
instead of raspberry cordial.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:27.960
It was my fault because I forgot that I
put the bottle there after the last meeting.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:31.940
But didn't you know the difference yourself?

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:34.280
I never tasted it.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:38.550
I meant to be so hospitable to Diana.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:45.700
Diana got awfully sick and had to go home.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:51.390
I tried to keep her but Diana
was angry and laughing, and went home.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.330
That's why you were so worried!

00:18:55.850 --> 00:19:02.900
Mrs. Lynde heard that Diana just laughed
silly-like and went to sleep for hours.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:07.900
Her mother smelled her breath
and knew she was drunk.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:12.530
And poor Diana had a fearful
headache all day yesterday.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:17.260
Mrs. Barry will never believe
but what I did it on purpose.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:21.660
I should think she would better punish Diana

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:24.560
for being so greedy as to drink
three glassfuls of anything.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:29.930
Why, three of those big glasses would have
made her sick even if it was just cordial.

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.320
Well, this story will be a nice handle

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:38.940
for those folks who are so down
on me for making currant wine.

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:42.280
Although I haven't made any for three years.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:45.510
I just kept that bottle for sickness.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.700
There, there, child, don't cry.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.630
I can't see as you were to blame
although I'm sorry it happened so.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.680
Yes, it's not your fault.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.690
I must cry.

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:01.480
The stars in their courses fight against me.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:05.030
Diana and I are parted forever.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:12.300
I little dreamed of this when first we
swore our vows of friendship.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.530
Don't be foolish, Anne.

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:20.440
Mrs. Barry will think better of it when
she finds you're not to blame.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:23.770
All right. I'll go and tell Mrs. Barry.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:26.750
Since It was my fault.

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:28.080
Marilla!

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:31.460
Don't worry. I shall return with good news.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:36.360
Marilla went out full of confidence.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:44.330
But the sun began to set and Marilla
had yet to return to Green Gables.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.490
Oh, Marilla, I know by your
face that it's been no use.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.460
Mrs. Barry indeed!

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:04.930
Of all the unreasonable women
I ever saw she's the worst.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:11.180
I told her it was all a mistake
and you weren't to blame,

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:14.720
but she just simply didn't believe me.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:24.030
And she rubbed it well in
about my currant wine

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:28.290
and how I'd always said it couldn't
have the least effect on anybody.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:30.380
I just told her plainly

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.990
that currant wine wasn't meant to
be drunk three tumblerfuls at a time

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:40.060
and that if a child of mine was so greedy
I'd sober her up with a right good spanking.

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.350
What do you want?

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:55.540
Mrs. Barry, please forgive me.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:22:01.070
I... I did not... mean to intoxicate Diana.

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:03.010
How could I?

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:06.940
Just imagine if you were a
poor little orphan girl

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:12.110
that kind people had adopted and you had
just one bosom friend in all the world.

00:22:12.110 --> 00:22:15.830
Do you think you would
intoxicate her on purpose?

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:19.700
I thought it was only raspberry cordial.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.350
I was firmly convinced it
was raspberry cordial.

00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:27.110
Oh, please don't say that you won't
let Diana play with me any more.

00:22:27.580 --> 00:22:33.720
If you do, you will cover my life
with a dark cloud of woe.

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:38.680
I don't think you are a fit little girl
for Diana to associate with.

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:41.540
You'd better go home and behave yourself.

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:46.710
Won't you let me see Diana
just once to say farewell?

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:50.320
Diana has gone over to
Carmody with her father.

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:05.210
My last hope is gone.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:20.230
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:22.570
Anne Returns to School

00:24:22.580 --> 00:24:23.870
Please watch!
